     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi everyone!<div><br></div><div>I have this model: </div><div>model.corr&lt;- &#39;<br><br>STRESS =~ S1+S2+S3<br>EMOCAO =~ EM1+ EM2 +EM3+ EM4<br>INTER =~ I1+I2+I3+I4<br>CRIATIVIDADE =~ C1+C2+C3+C4<br>TREIN =~ T1+T2+T3+T4<br clear=\"all\"><div><br></div><div>&#39;</div><div><br></div><div>I need to create a new model with fix the correlation between STRESS and EMOCAO at 1.</div><div><br></div><div>I want to do this because I will use anova at two model to know if I have discriminant validity. (my VME square is low than correlation between some factors) <span style=\"color:rgb(17,17,17);font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;font-size:12pt;white-space:pre-wrap\"> </span>[Anderson &amp; Gerbin (1988)]</div><div><br></div><div>So, how can I fix those two factors?</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div>-- <br><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Danilo Monteiro Ribeiro</div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"text-align:justify\"><font face=\"ArialMT, Arial, sans-serif\" color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;line-height:17px\"><b>Ph. D in Computer Science at Informatics Center of UFPE, Brasil</b></span></font></div><div><b>Software Engineering Researcher at Zup Innovation and Itaú.</b></div><div><br></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div><br> <table style=\"border-top:1px solid #d3d4de\">\r\n\t<tr>\r\n      <td style=\"width:55px;padding-top:18px\"><a href=\"https://www.avast.com/sig-email?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=link&amp;utm_campaign=sig-email&amp;utm_content=webmail\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.avast.com/sig-email?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dlink%26utm_campaign%3Dsig-email%26utm_content%3Dwebmail&amp;source=gmai